  },
  "note": "\"Owing to the withdrawals of four nominated candidates for urban councillors in Keady, there will be no contest.\" The paper lists \"the new councillors for three years\"; Watters, M'Bride and Smyth are styled J.P. James Vallely succeeded P. Comiskey, who did not offer himself for re-election. The Armagh Guardian (13 January 1911, p. 2): \"In Keady a contest has been avoided by candidates retiring.\" The polling day for the other councils was Monday 16 January 1911."
